    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27041" root="طلو and طلى" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَطْلِىٌّ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَلِىٌّ</span>: ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَلًا</span>; and see the
fem., with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَلْيَآءُ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمْرٌ مَطْلِىٌّ</span>
(assumed tropical:)  <i>A dubious and obscure affair,</i> or <i>case:</i> as though
it were smeared over with that which involved it.
(TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُودٌ مَطْلِىٌّ</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>A stick,</i> or <i>rod,</i> or
<i>branch, not stript of the peel</i> or <i>bark.</i> (TA.)

